SUMMARY:Author Talk: Karin Martin on "Get Plum Island"
LOCATION:Boston Public Library\, 700 Boylston Street\, Boston\, MA 02116
DESCRIPTION:Join University of Michigan professor Karin Martin for a conver
 sation about her new book Get Plum Island!: Place and Politics in Massachu
 setts’s Ten-Year Fight Over the Parker River National Wildlife Refuge. T
 he book tells the story of how the USFWS became interested in establishing
  a national wildlife refuge in Massachusetts\, why Essex County became a p
 remiere location\, and how local communities and the state nearly succeede
 d in having the refuge abolished. Instead\, after rounds of Congressional 
 hearings and pocket veto by President Truman\, a compromise was reached\, 
 reducing the refuge to about half its original size\, and yet preserving t
 he wonderful\, vibrant refuge we know today.\nhttps://bpl.bibliocommons.co
 m/events/6ab28390101eb7003f320c4c\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.ci
 ty/boston/
URL:https://bpl.bibliocommons.com/events/6ab28390101eb7003f320c4c
END:VEVENT
